WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.220 --> 00:00:05.730
Kim Rhode: Shooting sports were something that were
passed down traditionally my family.

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:09.900
My grandfather was a houndsman and he taught
my dad and my dad taught my mom and

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:13.440
before I knew what I was going to my
first Olympics and walked away with a

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:18.620
gold medal. Now I look back, six
Olympics later, and I'm still going strong

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:20.939
Hillsdale I've heard through the

00:00:20.939 --> 00:00:25.350
grapevine, through various people. It's just 
been really this fantastic place where

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:30.269
people are very like-minded, very much
about the Constitution, very much about

00:00:30.269 --> 00:00:35.160
Second Amendment, and very much about
shooting and heritage sports. The shooting

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:38.430
sports facility is gorgeous. One of the
things that really struck me because I

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:43.730
think coming from LA we don't have all
the openness, and how open it is, how

00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:49.559
beautiful and how well maintained, as
well as the facility itself and all the

00:00:49.559 --> 00:00:53.579
different things that they offer in the
forms of shooting--from sporting clays

00:00:53.579 --> 00:00:59.160
to five stand, to skeet, to bunker. I mean,
it really is impressive. I have to say I

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:03.930
am blown away not only at the facility
but what they're doing here and the

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:09.080
future that they're making for the
shooting sports and for the kids.

